{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'TODO|TBD|unknown|1–4|10 seconds|0\\\\.1|first script|1\\\\.05M|50|Source Information|Testing Feedback|Engine Feedback|Prompt Feedback' PLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"5:This plan is for gpt-6.1-sol ultracode with the supplied 1.05M context window. Use that capacity to understand the engine and integration contracts together, keep the whole game's state model coherent [... omitted end of long line]\n17:- The [MAME CVS driver](https://github.com/mamedev/mame/blob/master/src/mame/misc/cvs.cpp) corroborates the Century release, color-raster display and speech hardware. Exact music, scoring tables and t [... omitted end of long line]\n21:**The title is yours.** Silently brainstorm 50 playful riffs on the source's name and select one with an actual random-number generator. Do not substitute a favorite after drawing. Use the result cons [... omitted end of long line]\n35:| AI Hub co-op | 1–4 players in the same siege, with an authoritative host and a valid dedicated-host path. Online transport comes from the Hub. |\n36:| Attract mode | A looping AI demonstration spanning all three acts, entered after exactly 10 seconds of title/menu inactivity. |\n97:Make custom assets for player ships, every enemy, the evolving fortress, radiator sections, gravity anchors, boss components, ground carriages, pickups and the title composition. Use the generic asset [... omitted end of long line]\n139:Use a clean simulation instance or a clean run reset for attract. At 10 seconds without meaningful input on the title/menu, begin a compressed AI tour: free flight, gravity escape, core defense, then  [... omitted end of long line]\n160:| Audio | Native procedural sound/music and custom `audio.instrument`; route through music, SFX and voice buses. Native music defaults to 0.5, so override the initial value to 0.1. |\n206:1. Include the released `session.js` **unmodified**, as the first script in the document head immediately after the charset metadata. Follow the current importer requirement exactly. Inline engine/gam [... omitted end of long line]\n235:3. **Full mechanical content.** Add all threat behaviors, authored beats, upgrades, shared objectives, couch joining and online intents/snapshots. Gate: every mechanic has a reachable normal-play intr [... omitted end of long line]\n257:| Attract | Before 10 seconds it has not started; at the threshold it starts. It tours all acts and loops. Test exit with each meaningful input class and confirm no score/save pollution or input leaka [... omitted end of long line]\n258:| Audio | OfflineAudioContext or analyser tests produce finite, non-silent music/SFX/voice with bounded levels; new-profile music defaults to 0.1; mute/bus controls and pause/end cleanup work. Report  [... omitted end of long line]\n267:Use existing browsers and the installed Playwright version; do not download browsers or install system packages. Keep one or two browser processes open, using several pages/contexts for co-op. Prefer  [... omitted end of long line]\n269:Visually inspect a small purposeful set: title, each act during a representative threat, final boss, results, controller focus/dev sliders, readable credits, and touch framing. Verify the 1080p ten-fo [... omitted end of long line]\n277:Provide an About/Credits flow with clearly readable pages for **Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback**. Drive it and the builder's required exit interview from the [... omitted end of long line]\n283:- The chosen title came from 50 candidates and an actual random draw; all naming matches the builder's own brief.\n291:- No TODOs, stubbed menu actions, fake online screens, starter-game leftovers, inaccessible act, unimplemented upgrade or unfinished ending remains.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path('PLAN.md')\ntext = p.read_text()\nassert text.strip()\nassert 'gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261106-021146' not in text\nassert '/home/' not in text\nassert '/tmp/' not in text\nquestions = [\n    'What did you like most about this prompt?',\n    'What was confusing?',\n    'What was the hardest thing to do?',\n    'What would you change in this prompt?',\n]\ninterview = json.loads(Path('planner-exit-interview.json').read_text())\nassert isinstance(interview, list) and len(interview) == len(questions)\nfor item, question in zip(interview, questions, strict=True):\n    assert set(item) == {'question', 'answer'}\n    assert item['question'] == question\n    assert isinstance(item['answer'], str) and item['answer'].strip()\nprint(f'Passed: plan constraints and 4 interview entries; plan has {len(text.split()):,} words.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
